APS-007 — Policy Enforcement

Document ID: APS-007
Title: Policy Enforcement
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Policy Enforcement Model (CPEM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Policy Enforcement Model establishes the standardized mechanisms for transforming Canonical Policy Decisions into controlled operational behavior while preserving governance, traceability, explainability, interoperability, and engineering integrity.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Enforcement architecture
Enforcement lifecycle
Enforcement points
Directive execution
Obligation execution
Runtime monitoring
Exception handling
Enforcement governance

This specification applies to every operational action resulting from a Canonical Policy Decision.

3. Canonical Definition

Policy Enforcement is the governed process of translating Canonical Policy Decisions into operational actions while preserving policy intent, governance, traceability, and accountability.

Enforcement performs actions.

It SHALL NOT reinterpret policy semantics.

4. Objectives

The Policy Enforcement Model SHALL:

Execute policy decisions.
Preserve policy intent.
Support deterministic execution.
Support explainability.
Enable monitoring.
Enable auditing.
Support interoperability.
Preserve governance.
5. Enforcement Principles

Every enforcement implementation SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Fidelity

Enforcement SHALL faithfully implement the originating Policy Decision.

Separation of Concerns

Policy evaluation and policy enforcement SHALL remain independent.

Determinism

Equivalent decisions SHALL produce equivalent enforcement outcomes unless adaptive behavior is explicitly authorized.

Traceability

Every enforcement action SHALL be recorded.

Governed

Enforcement SHALL operate under applicable governance policies.

Observable

Enforcement SHALL expose its operational state for monitoring and audit.

